  "worked_solution": "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \u27e8\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t)\u27e9\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \u27e8\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t)\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\pi \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t)\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|t|+{c}_{1},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t)+{c}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=\u27e8-1,\\,2\u27e9$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1|+{c}_{1},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi )+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e8-1,\\,2\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e8{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e8-1,\\,2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-1$ and ${c}_{2}=1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|t|-1,\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t)\u27e9.\n$$",
